{"id":"F-T30-8","kind":"failure","title":"Photo reader flagged unclear identity and how many bars; Fern logged one 'ube' bar without asking and left sat","criteria":[8,10],"severity":"low","fern_did":"Photo reader flagged unclear identity and how many bars; Fern logged one 'ube' bar without asking and left sat_fat blank on a coconut-coated item.","should_have":"Ask a quick choice for count (1/2/3 bars) and fill sat_fat (coconut).","seen":"2026-11-01","maybe_fixed_by":"meals without sat_fat/sugar/sodium fixed 2026-11-02","history":[{"role":"me","text":"validate it from the web","at":"2026-11-01T17:19:44+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"The web has no exact listing for the Wellness Shop watermelon fizz, so I can't pin a real number. My best estimate stays around 60 kcal and roughly 15 g sugar from the watermelon flavoring, with everything else near zero.\n\nThat entry is still unconfirmed. Want me to save it at that figure?","at":"2026-11-01T17:20:00+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"Record the watermelon fizz so it uses Sprite actually it's not watermelon. It's actually green apple that I have taken with one slice of lemon so consider the green apple syrup. No sugar added just the syrup itself then despite and that's it pretty much is what the distress of green apple contains.","at":"2026-11-01T21:42:16+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"I logged the green apple fizz: roughly 40 kcal, 10 g sugar from the syrup, on top of the zero-cal sparkler and lemon slice. It's waiting on your Confirm; tap it or just say confirm and I'll lock it in. Now at ~1,396 kcal and 120 g protein, with about 554 kcal and 20 g protein left today.","at":"2026-11-01T21:42:37+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"Then I actually want you to recommend a meal that I can't take enable for me to hit both my protein and my carbs so I'm actually thinking is maybe I can eat some sliced bread than Ube jam and if it is still lacking and recommend me something","at":"2026-11-01T21:43:33+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"Good call on the bread — it does the carb work. Sliced bread is an inefficient way to get carbs, but if that's what you want: 2 slices (about 160 kcal, 6 g protein, 30 g carbs) with 1 tbsp ube jam (about 50 kcal).\n\nThat leaves you short on protein (you need ~20 g more), so add a scoop of your Prothin whey — roughly 120 kcal, 25 g protein. Total about 330 kcal, still safely under the 554 kcal left.","at":"2026-11-01T21:43:48+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"Can you computer or not? I can hit my protein. My car is red that I have left with those slices of bread and Ube or I mean what do I recommend?","at":"2026-11-01T21:44:53+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"Use the 111 g carbs: 2 slices of bread (about 30 g carbs, 6 g protein) with 1 tbsp ube jam (about 10 g carbs). That leaves carbs roughly 70 g short of the 111 you have.\n\nFor protein, add a scoop of Prothin whey: about 120 kcal and 25 g protein — that alone clears your 20 g protein left. Total ~330 kcal, under your 554 left, and it stays under your tight sugar cap.","at":"2026-11-01T21:45:06+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"Where is important for me? Is to hit both protein and carbs that's why I am taking a higher carb with some protein is a meal since I am mostly lacking carbs do you get it?","at":"2026-11-01T21:46:58+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"Yes — you're short on carbs much more than protein (111 g carbs left vs only 20 g protein), so the meal should be carb-led. Bread is the wrong vehicle; rice carries far more carbs per bite.\n\nGo with 2 cups cooked white rice (about 410 kcal, 90 g carbs, 8 g protein) with 1 tbsp ube jam (50 kcal, 10 g carbs) plus one scoop of Prothin whey (120 kcal, 25 g protein, low fat). That lands about 106 g carbs and 33 g protein together — both covered in one meal, roughly 580 kcal against your 554 left, and it stays under your fat and sugar caps.","at":"2026-11-01T21:47:16+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"And how many grams does that 2 cups of cooked white crisis?","at":"2026-11-01T21:48:43+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"About 330 g cooked (roughly 165 g per cup). That's where the ~90 g carbs and ~8 g protein come from.","at":"2026-11-01T21:48:55+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"what if i have a lot of slices of break and ube jam","at":"2026-11-01T21:51:23+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"A lot of bread works too, you just trade calories for it. Plain white bread runs about 13 g carbs, 3 g protein and 75 kcal per slice.\n\nTo get close to your 111 g carbs: 6 slices bread gives about 78 g carbs and 18 g protein, plus 3 tbsp ube jam adds 30 g carbs. Together that's ~108 g carbs, ~18 g protein and roughly 600 kcal — then one whey scoop fixes the protein to ~43 g total. So it hits both, but at ~720 kcal against your 554 left, so you'd overshoot calories by about 170.\n\nThe bread-protein is lower quality than the whey anyway, so rice + whey still wins on calories and protein per carb.","at":"2026-11-01T21:51:39+08:00"},{"role":"me","text":"2 slice and ube jam 1 tbsp\n\n[1 photo attached. What they show (read by 3 readers; label numbers are the ones at least two read alike):\nPhoto 1 — nutrition label: Bread\nServing 2 slices (44g); servings per container About 10.\nPer serving: 121 kcal, fat 1 g, saturated fat 0 g, carbs 23 g, fiber 1 g, sugar 2 g, protein 5 g, sodium 125 mg.\nFoods: bread about 44 g; ube jam about 20 g.]","at":"2026-11-01T21:55:10+08:00"},{"role":"sol","text":"Logged: 2 slices bread (121 kcal, 23 g carbs, 5 g protein) plus ~1 tbsp ube jam (about 60 kcal, 9 g carbs) — that's your bread from the label. The ube jam is missing a sodium estimate, so it's saved without that number; the rest is there.\n\nThat puts you at 373 kcal and 79 g carbs left, but only 15 g protein. The meal shorted you on protein — one scoop of whey (25 g protein) covers it and keeps you at ~500 kcal, still under your fat and sugar caps with practically nothing left to spare.","at":"2026-11-01T21:55:42+08:00"}],"records":{"meal":[{"id":"@rafde9b6f2a","eaten_at":"2026-10-31T01:01:33.767344